  "analysis_conventions": {
   "fallback_status": "T9 is confirmatory only if k* exists for both objall and cam; T10 is run exactly as specified only if k* exists for cont. Otherwise the same computation is run at k_used and reported as descriptive unless the lead decides otherwise (plan risk 4)",
   "T9": "test split (v2 odd seeds) primary, transfer descriptive. For P_obj (objall, tau_O) and P_cam (cam, tau_C) at k*: statistic = scene median over test scenes; null draw r (r = 1..40) uses the same matched component set on every scene (numpy default_rng(k) per scene), its statistic = scene median of that set; null rank p = (1 + #{null >= observed}) / 41; pass = observed above the 95th percentile of the 40 null medians for both, and scene-median leakage (lambda_O = dpose_rel of the P_obj patch, lambda_C = dF_rel of the P_cam patch) <= 0.2 for both; p_T9 = max(p_O, p_C). Boundary rule applied to F (primary); no-rule values reported",
   "T5p": "identifiable test scenes in the unedited D run (boundary rule). d_s = (alpha_i - alpha_base) - mean over the 20 random projectors of (alpha_iii - alpha_base); H1 mean d > 0; one-sided scene bootstrap (2000, seed 0), p = (1 + #{bootstrap mean <= 0}) / 2001; g = 1.5 confirmatory, g = 2 secondary",
   "T10": "windows of results/u2/pose_windows.json pooled over Sintel, TUM-dynamics and Bonn; d_w = mean over the 20 frozen random head sets of RPE-R(c) - RPE-R(a); H1 mean d > 0; one-sided window bootstrap (2000, seed 0), p = (1 + #{bootstrap mean <= 0}) / 2001; per-set values descriptive",
   "U5a_success": "on identifiable test scenes (g = 1.5): mean d alpha >= 0.10, |mean d beta| <= 0.03, mean d moving EPE <= +1 px, mean static EPE ratio - 1 <= 0.05 for (i); mean d beta >= 0.10 and |mean d alpha| <= 0.03 for (ii)",
   "U5b_success": "T10 significant after the lead's Holm correction; Kubric test D: mean (1 - e_a) >= 0.5 mean (1 - e_d) with e normalised by the unedited D run; mean d moving EPE of (a) <= +1 px. The contamination-null check (D - B RPE-R CI includes 0) uses the behaviour track's T8; this track also reports the Kubric test D - B RPE-R CI from its own unedited runs (descriptive)",
   "component_ranking_note": "rank orders come from the fit screens, which used all moving query points (screens ran on 2026-10-20 before the boundary rule was implemented in the readout); joint, k*, necessity and every test metric apply the boundary rule (primary) and also store the no-rule value"
  },
